    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW264xQ1rraVxBDBip6TeNyfG)_\n\nStacked on #374 (base is its branch; it uses `sp-writing-projects`). Retarget to `main` after #374 merges.\n\n## Cause\n- `projectile-project-search-path` was set twice in `sp-workspaces.el`: `~/Documents/writing/` and `~/.config/` in `:init`, `sp-git-dir` and `sp-src-dir` in `:custom`.\n- `:custom` runs after `:init`, so the writing folder was never searched (read from the code, not run in Emacs).\n\n## Changes\n- The `:init` value is removed; `:custom` now holds `sp-git-dir`, `sp-src-dir` and `(cons sp-writing-projects 1)`.\n  - Depth 1: each direct subfolder of the writing folder with a `.git` is a project.\n  - `~/.config/` was only in the overridden value, so it is not searched, as before.\n- Doc `sp-workspaces.org` updated: where Projectile looks, the empty `.projectile` file for non-git folders, and the one-off `M-x projectile-discover-projects-in-search-path`.\n\n## After merging\n- Run `M-x projectile-discover-projects-in-search-path` once.\n\n## Not verified\n- Not run in Emacs (none in the container).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCtkuUzuiths11Hu1j)_",
